0..77 Comment "// An atom named inside the abstraction that binds it (Fernández and Gabbay,"
78..157 Comment "// _Nominal rewriting_, I&C 2007, § 2; Pitts, _Nominal Sets_, CUP 2013, § 4)."
158..237 Comment "// Inside `bind a . t` the name `a` is the atom `a`, and outside it a variable."
238..313 Comment "// Admission re-mints an atom with the abstraction that binds it, so a rule"
314..391 Comment "// naming the channel its restriction abstracts is one rule whatever the atom"
392..466 Comment "// is called: matching, the critical pairs and the kernel\'s replay read an"
467..543 Comment "// occurrence by the number of abstractions between it and its binder. Where"
544..621 Comment "// a port takes an atom, a term can name one, and a freshness condition there"
622..695 Comment "// is not decided yet (#1900): `pathological/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr`."
697..773 Comment "/// A send on a restricted channel, which no process outside the restriction"
774..851 Comment "/// can receive: the process never moves, so it is the inert one. The checker"
852..928 Comment "/// orients the law and the kernel replays the verdict; a restriction naming"
929..988 Comment "/// its channel `b` normalizes by the law written over `a`."
989..991 Other "@["
992..1002 Other "normalizes"
1002..1003 Other "("
1003..1004 StringLit "\""
1004..1035 StringLit "nu(bind b . out(b, nil)) ~> nil"
